UNIT escape_property
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 1a681329e2db069b1a3348780bc6c8d749a36ffcdca1f97da4b00b7b2eb61c6d
SIG escape_property(v: any): string
NOTE default export (the real code is the named `export const escapeProperty = (v) => …` of a larger module; the
  reconstruction default-exports one plain function)
ABI text=string (UTF-16 code units); R1 is applied per code unit. Every ESCAPES member is one ASCII code unit, so surrogate
  pairs and an unpaired surrogate half are never split or altered — the js widening admits such text (the primary excludes it), and no normalization occurs. The result is a new string.
ENVELOPE widening: the argument slot accepts any JS value, converted to text FIRST by the language's string conversion
  (String(v)) and then escaped by R1. That conversion is: a missing argument or undefined -> "undefined"; null -> "null";
  booleans -> "true"/"false"; numbers -> the shortest round-trip decimal (exponent form "1e+21" and "1e-7" outside
  [1e-6, 1e21)), -0 -> "0", NaN -> "NaN", Infinity -> "Infinity", -Infinity -> "-Infinity"; bigint -> its decimal
  digits without a suffix; a boxed String/Number/Boolean -> its primitive's text; an Array -> its elements, each
  converted the same way (undefined, null and holes -> empty), joined with "," — so every separator comma is then
  escaped to "%2C"; a RegExp -> "/source/flags"; a plain object -> "[object Object]"; Set -> "[object Set]"; Map ->
  "[object Map]"; a Uint8Array -> its bytes in decimal joined with ","; a Node Buffer -> its bytes DECODED AS UTF-8 (the
  Buffer's own toString); a Symbol -> "Symbol(description)". An object whose own toString is not callable, and whose
  valueOf (own or inherited) does not return a primitive, -> throws "Cannot convert object to primitive value" (also when
  such an object is an Array element). No JSON rendering is used (that is the anchor's toCommandValue; see the report).
  Extra positional arguments are ignored.
MECHANISM conversion = String(v) as the first operation (not `${v}`, which throws on a Symbol; not v.toString(), which
  throws on null/undefined). R1 = String.prototype.replace with each ESCAPES pin, in the order %, CR, LF, colon, comma
  (percent FIRST, so the "%" inserted by a later replacement is never re-escaped — R3), or equivalently one pass over
  code units mapping through ESCAPES. Replacement texts are constant strings with no "$" patterns.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex PCT = /%/g CITED R1 ESCAPES "%" -> "%25" — must run first (R3)
PINNED regex CR = /\r/g CITED R1 ESCAPES CR -> "%0D"
PINNED regex LF = /\n/g CITED R1 ESCAPES LF -> "%0A"
PINNED regex COLON = /:/g CITED R1 ESCAPES ":" -> "%3A"
PINNED regex COMMA = /,/g CITED R1 ESCAPES "," -> "%2C"
PROVENANCE rederive@c41c5fcd84e0 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs line 119 — the real source; this file states dialect and envelope
  only, no behavior.
